{"name":"Gull Feather","hex":"#c2c2bc","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"gull","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A seabird of the genus Larus or of the subfamily Larinae.","Any of various pierid butterflies of the genus Cepora."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A cheating trick; a fraud.","A stupid animal."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/gull"},{"term":"feather","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A branching, hair-like structure that grows on the bodies of birds, used for flight, swimming, protection and display.","Long hair on the lower legs of a dog or horse, especially a draft horse, notably the Clydesdale breed. Narrowly only the rear hair."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or furnish with feathers;  to fletch.","To adorn, as if with feathers; to fringe."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/feather"}],"entries":[{"title":"Gull","blocks":[{"text":"Gulls, informally called seagulls, are seabirds of the subfamily Larinae. They are most closely related to terns and skimmers, and are placed with them in the family Laridae. They are also related, more distantly, to auks and skuas, and more distantly still to waders. Until the 21st century, most gulls were placed in the genus Larus, but that arrangement is now considered polyphyletic, leading to the readoption and revision of several genera."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b9/Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG/330px-Herring_Gull_%28Larus_argentatus%29%2C_Brighton%2C_England.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gull","wikidata":"Q2699803"},{"title":"Feather","blocks":[{"text":"Feathers are epidermal growths that form a distinctive outer covering, or plumage, on both avian (bird) and some non-avian dinosaurs and other archosaurs. They are the most complex integumentary structures found in vertebrates and an example of a complex evolutionary novelty. They are among the characteristics that distinguish the extant birds from other living groups."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/80/Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg/330px-Types_de_plumes._-_Larousse_pour_tous%2C_-1907-1910-.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feather","wikidata":"Q81025"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/1280px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/21/Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg/500px-Armenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Immature (probably 2nd year) Armenian gull in flight, flying over Lake Sevan","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AArmenian_Gull_Juvenile_in_flight%2C_Sevan_lake.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg/500px-Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/73/Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg/500px-Larus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"The Pacific gull is a large white-headed gull with a distinctively heavy bill.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALarus_pacificus_Bruny_Island.jpg"},{"srcset":"https